# Signed approvals, part: the harness closes its own process
# (docs/steps/signed-approvals/parts/process-hardening.md).

# ------------------------------------------------------------- Linux

[break] the-process-stays-dumpable
rule: On Linux every process of the binary makes itself not dumpable before it reads anything, so that another process of its user can neither attach to it nor open its memory, environment or program's link.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/harden.rs
find: libc::prctl(libc::PR_SET_DUMPABLE, NONE, NONE, NONE, NONE)
replace: libc::prctl(libc::PR_GET_DUMPABLE, NONE, NONE, NONE, NONE)
os: linux
packages: cineris-sandbox, cineris-cli
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox::it harden::sys_a_closed_process_keeps_out_another_process_of_its_user
    cineris-cli::system hardened::sys_the_binary_closes_its_own_process

[break] a-word-counts-for-any-process
rule: A harness's word counts for the process that made it, as the kernel names it, started when the word says, and for no other: not for another process of the line.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/session.rs
find: word.pid == pid &&
replace:
os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox session::sys::tests::a_word_counts_only_for_the_process_that_gave_it

[break] the-launcher-drops-the-word
rule: The sandbox launcher, which marks every descriptor it holds to be closed when it becomes the command, lets the harness's word pass, so that a nested run inside the sandbox reads its session's stores.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/launch.rs
find: crate::session::channel::inherit(*word);
replace:
os: linux
packages: cineris-sandbox, cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox::it confined::sys_the_harnesss_word_passes_the_launcher

[break] a-hidden-process-of-this-user-ends-the-line
rule: A process of this user that /proc does not show (hidepid hides a harness that closed itself from its own commands) is not known on a line of parents, and refuses; only another user's, or one that is gone, ends the line.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/session.rs
find: Some(true) => Seen::Hidden,
replace: Some(true) => Seen::Unseen,
os: linux
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox session::sys::tests::a_process_proc_does_not_show_is_told_by_whose_it_is

# ----------------------------------------------------------- Windows

[break] the-process-list-keeps-reading-its-memory
rule: On Windows the harness's process gives its user and OWNER RIGHTS only to wait for it, ask it the limited questions and end it: reading its memory is left out.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/harden.rs
find: SYNCHRONIZE | PROCESS_QUERY_LIMITED_INFORMATION | PROCESS_TERMINATE
replace: SYNCHRONIZE | PROCESS_QUERY_LIMITED_INFORMATION | PROCESS_TERMINATE | 0x0010
os: windows
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox::it harden::sys_a_closed_process_keeps_out_another_process_of_its_user

[break] a-thread-made-later-keeps-the-default-list
rule: On Windows a thread the harness makes after it closed itself gives itself the threads' list as it starts, so that no process of the user can set its context, suspend it or queue work to it.
file: crates/cineris-sandbox/src/harden.rs
find: if reason != DLL_THREAD_ATTACH
replace: if reason == DLL_THREAD_ATTACH
os: windows
caught-by:
    cineris-sandbox::it harden::sys_a_closed_process_keeps_out_another_process_of_its_user
